# Closed octahedron (V=6 E=12 F=8, sphere) with integer coordinates.
# Opposite faces, e.g. face 1 (x y z) in x+y+z=2 and face 7 (mx mz my) in
# x+y+z=-2, have overlapping axis-aligned bounding boxes but lie on
# parallel, disjoint planes. The old AABB heuristic wrongly reported an
# intersection; correct embedding audit yields ok.
v x 2 0 0
v mx -2 0 0
v y 0 2 0
v my 0 -2 0
v z 0 0 2
v mz 0 0 -2
f x y z
f y mx z
f mx my z
f my x z
f x mz y
f y mz mx
f mx mz my
f my mz x
